{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 7, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "Hark fair traveler of distant lands prepare thy soul for Japan’s wondrous realm  \nWhere cherry blooms do dance in spring’s soft breath and mountains stand as ancient kings  \nThy journey starts in Kyoto where temples whisper tales of emperors long gone  \nThou shalt walk the mossy paths of Arashiyama where bamboo sings to thee alone  \nAt dawn thou shalt behold the golden glow of Kinkaku Ji its mirror face aglow  \nThen feast on noodles steaming bright as stars in Nishiki Market’s bustling row  \n\nThence to Osaka where the streets do laugh and food doth call like minstrels sweet  \nThou shalt taste takoyaki hot and bold as thunder in a summer’s heat  \nThen climb the tower high and see the land as if the gods did paint it true  \nWith lanterns bright as fireflies dancing through the twilight’s fading hue  \n\nTo Nara the deer shall bow to thee as if thou wert a lord of old  \nTheir eyes do hold the wisdom of the ages in their gentle gaze untold  \nThou shalt tread the halls of Todaiji where Buddha sleeps in bronze so grand  \nAnd feel the breath of centuries in every stone in every strand  \n\nThen haste to Mount Fuji its crown of snow doth pierce the heavens clear  \nThy soul shall tremble at its might as dawn doth paint it gold and sheer  \nAt Hakone the hot springs warm thy bones as mist doth veil the sacred lake  \nAnd in the ryokan thou shalt sleep as stars above do watch and wake  \n\nTo Tokyo the city bright where neon sings and silence hides in plain  \nThou shalt find a temple quiet where the wind doth weave a sacred chain  \nIn Shibuya the crowds do flow like rivers born of human will  \nYet in Shinjuku’s quiet nook thou shalt find peace against the thrill  \n\nAt last to Nikko where the gods do dwell in wood and stone and stream  \nThy heart shall swell with awe as shrines do gleam like dreams that never dream  \nThy journey ends not with thy feet but with thy spirit lifted high  \nFor Japan doth leave a mark no time nor tide can ever deny  \n\nGo forth brave soul and tread thy path with wonder as thy guide  \nAnd when thou returnest home thou shalt carry Japan inside", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.09076494723558426}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0023813480511307716}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -1.7260669469833374}, {"token": " traveler", "logprob": -0.08751427382230759}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.9759387969970703}, {"token": " distant", "logprob": -0.012501212768256664}, {"token": " lands", "logprob": -0.3132893741130829}, {"token": " prepare", "logprob": -0.942206621170044}, {"token": " thy", "logprob": -0.004626878537237644}, {"token": " soul", "logprob": -0.09130227565765381}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.0017909454181790352}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.08950403332710266}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.3756369352340698}, {"token": " w", "logprob": -0.43847352266311646}, {"token": "ondrous", "logprob": -0.0021974719129502773}, {"token": " realm", "logprob": -1.3766196966171265}, {"token": "  \n", "logprob": -0.6936694383621216}, {"token": "Where", "logprob": -0.016294749453663826}, {"token": " cherry", "logprob": -0.005893591325730085}, {"token": " blooms", "logprob": -0.3007526397705078}, {"token": " do", "logprob": -0.0717279240489006}, {"token": " dance", "logprob": -0.4273478090763092}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.5102548599243164}, {"token": " spring", "logprob": -0.05141449719667435}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.08066713064908981}, {"token": " soft", "logprob": -0.1796042025089264}, {"token": " breath", "logprob": -0.3283047080039978}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0005571481888182461}, {"token": " mountains", "logprob": -0.2766542434692383}, {"token": " stand", "logprob": -0.4022642970085144}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -0.010796231217682362}, {"token": " ancient", "logprob": -0.0930226668715477}, {"token": " kings", "logprob": -0.5241208076477